cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Scan-to-Text: literal transcription and filing of scanned clinical documents"
message: >-
  If this software is useful in your work, a citation is appreciated.
  It is asked for, not required by the licence.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Braga"
    given-names: "Henrique Faria"
    website: "https://radioterapia.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drhenriquebraga/scan-to-text"
url: "https://radioterapia.ai"
abstract: >-
  A Windows application that watches the scanner folder of a radiotherapy
  reception desk and transcribes, literally, every document that arrives into
  Markdown, filed by patient, category and date, offline and unattended. Layout
  analysis is performed by Docling and character recognition by RapidOCR with
  PaddleOCR models, third-party components; this project builds the pipeline
  around them. Part of Braga HealthLab. Not a medical device, and not
  validated for clinical use.
keywords:
  - radiation therapy
  - radiotherapy
  - optical character recognition
  - clinical documentation
  - medical records
  - windows
  - offline
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
